    <LibraryPath>$(SolutionDir)shared\Library;$(LibraryPath)</LibraryPath>
    <IncludePath>$(ProjectDir)src;$(ProjectDir)src\include;$(IncludePath)</IncludePath>
    <!-- LTCG is off by default because it was measured and did not pay.
         Enable with /p:ShellEnableLTCG=true.

         It is correct: the VM smoke test passes 24/24 with it on. It saves
         9.5 KB of 1524 KB. What it does not do is show up in menu build
         latency. Across three VM runs of twenty samples each, the warm minimum
         was 45.0 ms with LTCG, 46.3 ms without, and 44.5 ms with it again,
         while two runs of the *same* LTCG binary gave medians of 61.7 ms and
         77.0 ms. The run-to-run spread swamps any effect.

         Note also what the harness can resolve: it times WM_CONTEXTMENU to the
         popup becoming visible, which is mostly Explorer's own message
         handling, window creation and painting. Our menu build is a fraction of
         it, so a real improvement in our code could be present and invisible
         here. That is an argument for better instrumentation, not for turning
         on whole-image codegen changes in a DLL that loads into Explorer on the
         strength of convention. -->
    <ShellEnableLTCG Condition="'$(ShellEnableLTCG)'==''">false</ShellEnableLTCG>
  </PropertyGroup>
